    "intro_html":  "Cottage pie is the original stretch a pound of beef dinner. Ground beef and a chopped vegetable base go under a thick blanket of mashed potato, the whole thing bakes until the top browns, and it cuts into clean squares which makes portioning almost too easy. Shepherd\u0027s pie is the lamb version; this is the beef one. Each square carries \u003cstrong\u003e{{protein}} grams of protein\u003c/strong\u003e and {{cal}} calories for about \u003cstrong\u003e${{cost_ps}}\u003c/strong\u003e (at everyday cost).",
